  "body": "The attribute is similar to DOM's class/classList which is spec'ed as\n\"When an element is created that has a class attribute or when an element’s class attribute is set, set the element’s classes to the new value, parsed.\"\nand\n\"The classList\nattribute must return the associated DOMTokenList object representing the context object’s classes.\"\n\nBut HTML spec doesn't seem to really say anything like that for sandbox attribute, other than the attribute is reflected, but nothing about parsing or so.\n\nWould be nice to have some common language for DOMTokenList handling (assuming DOMTokenList is mapped to content attributes consistently)\n",
